It is early in the morning.
I am waiting in the citizens' office.
The room is large and very full.
Many people are sitting here.
I have an appointment for the registration today.
That is very important.
I look at the screen on the wall.
My number is forty-two.
The screen is now showing the number thirty-eight.
I calculate briefly.
Thirty-nine, forty, forty-one...
Four people are still ahead of me.
So I still have time.
I drink my coffee.
The coffee is hot and feels good.
Suddenly the screen flashes.
It shows the number thirty-nine.
Only three people left.
Soon it is my turn.
